---
import './capacity.css';
const { kind, number, title } = Astro.props;
const stepped = kind === 'journey' || kind === 'overload';
---
<figure class="cap" data-capacity={kind} aria-label={title}>
  <figcaption><span class="cap-number">Figure {number}</span><span class="cap-title">{title}</span></figcaption>
  <div class="cap-panel">
    {kind === 'journey' && <>
      <p class="cap-model">Illustrative schedule · one application pool, two open connections</p>
      <div class="cap-metrics" data-live></div>
      <div class="cap-scene" data-live></div>
    </>}
    {kind === 'occupancy' && <>
      <p class="cap-model">Two stable workloads · both complete 100 requests/s</p>
      <div class="cap-occupancy">
        {[40,200].map(ms => <div class="cap-mean"><p><strong>{ms} ms</strong> mean borrow-to-release</p><div class="cap-squares" aria-label={`${ms/10} mean occupied connections`}>{Array.from({length:20},(_,i)=><span class:list={{filled:i<ms/10}} aria-hidden="true"></span>)}</div><p class="cap-equation">100/s × {ms/1000} s = <strong>{ms/10} occupied on average</strong></p></div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="cap-key">One filled square = one occupied connection in the mean. Empty squares are a common scale, not a pool limit.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'budget' && <>
      <p class="cap-model">Illustrative budget · 100 server connections · pool maximum 12 per app instance</p>
      <div class="cap-options"><label>Instances sharing this database <select data-instances><option value="4">4 running</option><option value="6">6 running</option><option value="10">6 new + 4 old during rollout</option></select></label></div>
      <div class="cap-budget" data-live></div>
    </>}
    {kind === 'overload' && <>
      <p class="cap-model">Illustrative burst · 7 requests at once · 2 execution places · 100 ms per request</p>
      <div class="cap-options"><label>Waiting policy <select data-policy><option value="bounded">Queue at most 2; refuse excess</option><option value="unbounded">Queue every arrival; keep expired work</option></select></label></div>
      <div class="cap-metrics" data-live></div>
      <div class="cap-scene" data-live></div>
    </>}
    {stepped && <>
      <p class="cap-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
      <div class="cap-controls" role="group" aria-label={`Playback for figure ${number}`}>
        <button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span>
      </div><div class="cap-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
    </>}
  </div>
  {kind === 'journey' && <details class="cap-alternative"><summary>Read the steps as text</summary><ol><li>Mina waits in the application. Two other requests occupy both connections.</li><li>The first request finishes and releases connection 1.</li><li>Mina borrows connection 1. No statement from her has reached the database yet.</li><li>A separate session H, outside this pool, holds an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE table lock on orders. Mina’s history statement waits for it; her connection stays occupied.</li><li>H ends its transaction and releases the lock. Mina’s statement runs.</li><li>The result is consumed and her connection is released. The second other request, an unrelated products read, continues throughout. No business rows change.</li></ol></details>}
  {kind === 'overload' && <details class="cap-alternative"><summary>Read the two outcomes as text</summary><p>With a two-request queue, requests 1–2 run immediately, 3–4 wait 100 ms, and 5–7 are refused immediately. All four admitted requests finish by 200 ms. With an unlimited queue and no expiry removal, 1–6 finish by 300 ms; request 7 starts at its 300 ms deadline and finishes at 400 ms, too late. These fixed service times are assumptions, not engine measurements.</p></details>}
</figure>

<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  const metric = (value, label) => `<div><strong>${value}</strong><span>${label}</span></div>`;
  const chip = (text, state='') => `<span class="cap-chip ${state}">${text}</span>`;
  const lane = (name, contents) => `<div class="cap-lane"><p class="cap-lane-name">${name}</p><div class="cap-lane-body">${contents}</div></div>`;
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-capacity]').forEach(root => {
    const kind = root.getAttribute('data-capacity');
    if (kind === 'journey') {
      const explanations = [
        'Mina has arrived, but both pool connections are borrowed. She waits in the application; the database has no statement from her.',
        'The first other request finishes. Connection 1 stays open and becomes idle. Mina is still shown in the queue, just before checkout.',
        'Mina borrows connection 1. It is occupied now, even before her statement reaches the database.',
        'Separate session H has acquired an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE table lock on orders. Mina’s SELECT waits for H while her pool connection stays occupied. B reads products, so that lock does not block B.',
        'H ends its transaction and releases the table lock. Mina’s SELECT can run. Pool occupancy did not change when the wait became execution.',
        'The application consumes the result and releases connection 1. It stays open for the next request. No shop row changed.'
      ];
      stepper(root, {steps:()=>6, draw:s=>{
        root.querySelector('.cap-metrics').innerHTML = metric(s<2?1:0,'queued requests') + metric(s===1||s===5?1:2,'occupied connections') + metric(s<1||s===4?2:1,'executing statements') + metric(s===3?1:0,'waiting statements');
        const first = s===0?'Other request A':s===1||s===5?'Idle':"Mina’s request";
        const db = s===0?'A executing':s===3?'Mina waiting for table lock':s===4?'Mina executing':'No statement on connection 1';
        root.querySelector('.cap-scene').innerHTML = lane('Application queue',s<2?chip('Mina · waiting','waiting'):'<span class="cap-empty">Empty</span>') + lane('Open pool connections',chip('C1 · '+first,s===1||s===5?'idle':'active')+chip('C2 · Other request B','active')) + '<p class="cap-boundary">↓ statements sent over borrowed connections</p>' + lane('Database statements',chip(db,s===3?'waiting':s===0||s===4?'active':'idle')+chip('B · products read executing','active')) + (s===3?lane('Separate session',chip('H · holds orders table lock · outside pool','waiting')):'');
        root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent = explanations[s];
      }});
    }
    if (kind === 'budget') {
      const select = root.querySelector('[data-instances]');
      const draw=()=>{
        const count=Number(select.value),app=count*12,total=app+20;
        root.querySelector('.cap-budget').innerHTML = `<p class="cap-equation">${count} × 12 + 10 workers + 10 operations = <strong>${total} slots budgeted</strong></p><div class="cap-budget-scale" aria-hidden="true"><span>0</span><span>100-slot ceiling ↓</span></div><div class="cap-budget-track" role="img" aria-label="${app} application slots, 10 worker slots and 10 operational slots against a 100-slot ceiling"><div class="cap-budget-bar" style="width:${total/1.4}%"><span style="flex:${app}" class="cap-app">${app}</span><span style="flex:10" class="cap-worker">10</span><span style="flex:10" class="cap-ops">10</span></div><span class="cap-ceiling"></span></div><p class="cap-key">Application pools · workers · operational allowance. The line marks 100.</p><p class="cap-budget-result ${total>100?'over':''}">${total>100?'40 over the budget. This overlap cannot retain the stated allowances.':`${100-total} slots remain unallocated. These are maxima, not a count of live connections.`}</p>`;
      }; select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();
    }
    if (kind === 'overload') {
      const select=root.querySelector('[data-policy]');
      const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw:s=>{
        const bounded=select.value==='bounded',t=s*100,max=bounded?4:7;
        const done=Math.min(s*2,max),running=s<Math.ceil(max/2)?Math.min(2,max-done):0,queued=Math.max(0,max-done-running);
        root.querySelector('.cap-metrics').innerHTML=metric(t+' ms','since burst')+metric(running,'running')+metric(queued,'queued')+metric(bounded?3:0,'refused');
        const groups={Running:[],Queued:[],Finished:[],Refused:[]};
        for(let i=1;i<=7;i++){
          let status=i>max?'Refused':i<=done?'Finished':i<=done+running?'Running':'Queued';
          const late=!bounded&&i===7&&s>=3;
          groups[status].push(chip(`R${i}${late?' · deadline passed':''}`,status==='Running'?(late?'waiting':'active'):status==='Refused'?'waiting':status==='Queued'?'queued': 'idle'));
        }
        root.querySelector('.cap-scene').innerHTML=Object.entries(groups).map(([name,list])=>lane(name,list.join('')||'<span class="cap-empty">None</span>')).join('');
        const boundedText=[
          'Two requests start. Two wait without borrowing a connection. The queue is full, so three get an immediate overload response. Each request has a 300 ms end-to-end deadline; maximum queue wait is 120 ms.',
          'R1 and R2 finish at 100 ms. R3 and R4 have waited 100 ms, within the 120 ms queue budget, and start now.',
          'All four admitted requests finish by 200 ms. Three callers already know their requests were refused and can follow the backoff policy.',
          'At 300 ms there is no burst work left to run. Refusals remain refusals; the figure does not silently retry them.',
          'The queue is empty and the four useful completions remain. The bounds made the burst’s cost explicit.'
        ];
        const unboundedText=[
          'Two requests start and five wait. This alternative has no queue-length limit or expiry removal. Service is still only two requests per 100 ms.',
          'R1 and R2 finish. R3 and R4 start; three requests still wait. Accepting more work did not add execution places.',
          'R3 and R4 finish. R5 and R6 start. R7 has already waited 200 ms.',
          'R5 and R6 finish at 300 ms. R7 starts just as its end-to-end deadline expires. The caller has no time left to use the result.',
          'R7 finishes at 400 ms, after its deadline. Seven database completions include one useless late result. Removing expired work would have avoided its last 100 ms of execution.'
        ];root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=(bounded?boundedText:unboundedText)[s];
      }});select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
    }
  });
</script>
